---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PipArt from '../components/PipArt.astro';
import { getLiveStats } from '../stats';

const live = await getLiveStats();

const repo = 'https://github.com/abhibansal60/abhibansal60.github.io';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How abhibansal.dev is built, tested and kept fast.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <p class="lede">How this site is built, and the checks that keep it fast and usable.</p>

    <h2>Quality gate</h2>
    <p>Every change goes through a pull request. A <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/.github/workflows/quality.yml`}>GitHub Action</a> builds the site and runs Lighthouse on six pages; if performance, accessibility, best practices or SEO drops below 90 on any of them, the check fails. When the gate was added on 25 September 2026, all six pages scored 99 or 100 in every category; current results are on the <a href={`${repo}/actions/workflows/quality.yml`}>workflow runs page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Built with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, static output, with a few small scripts and no framework runtime</li>
      <li>Schibsted Grotesk for text and B612 Mono for the console, both self-hosted</li>
      <li>GitHub Pages, deployed by a GitHub Action on every merge to main</li>
      <li>Every page works without JavaScript and respects reduced-motion settings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Live numbers</h2>
    <p>These come from the GitHub and PyPI APIs at build time, and the site rebuilds every night. If a source fails, its number is left out rather than shown stale.</p>
    {live.stats.length > 0 && (
      <dl class="live">
        {live.stats.map((st) => <div><dt>{st.label}</dt><dd>{st.value}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
    )}

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>Visits are counted with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which sets no cookies and collects no personal data. There is nothing to accept and no banner.</p>

    <h2>For agents</h2>
    <p>My profile is available as <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>, <a href="/llms-full.txt">llms-full.txt</a> and <a href="/resume.json">resume.json</a> (JSON Resume format), all generated from the same data as these pages.</p>
    <p>The same facts are served by a read-only MCP server at <code>https://pip.abhibansal60.workers.dev/mcp</code>, with tools for my profile, career timeline, systems built, projects, talk topics and contact details. To add it to Claude Code:</p>
    <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http abhinav https://pip.abhibansal60.workers.dev/mcp</code></pre>

    <h2>Ask Pip</h2>
    <p>Questions typed into the console on the home page go to a Cloudflare Worker. Common questions (contact, CV, the patent, location) are answered straight from the site's data. Anything else goes to a small Workers AI model that only sees the facts on this site, and plain code checks its answer before it is shown: it has to be short and about my work, or you get a polite "I only answer questions about Abhinav's work". Questions about jobs or pay, and attempts to change Pip's instructions, never reach the model. The model runs at most 250 times a day, well inside Cloudflare's free allowance, so it costs nothing.</p>

    <h2>Pip</h2>
    <div class="pip-note">
      <PipArt width={72} />
      <p>Pip is the site's plumber droid, drawn in SVG. It sits beside the headline on the home page; type <code>pip</code> in the console and it follows you around the site.</p>
    </div>

    <p><a href={repo}>Source on GitHub</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .live { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 2rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .live div { display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; }
  .live dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .live dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.4rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .pip-note { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: center; }
  .pip-note p { margin: 0; }
</style>
